{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1553931-caestus-pax-1e-vs-all-of-2e-team-tomorrow","id":1553931,"title":"Caestus Pax (1e) vs. all of 2e Team Tomorrow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-19T17:58:58-07:00","id":1553931,"title":"Caestus Pax (1e) vs. all of 2e Team Tomorrow","content":"As the title says, this is just a fun little versus debate. I'm imagining a sort of scenario where after traveling through a Flux Gate Caestus Pax (the 1st Edition leader of Team Tomorrow, in all his arrogant glory) arrives in the 2nd Edition version of Aberrant, believing that the Team Tomorrow he finds are imposters that have to be defeated (or at least, believes that <i>Cestus</i> Pax is an imposter mind-controlling the other Team Tomorrow members.) Cestus and the others meanwhile are looking at this evil clone of their leader, trying to figure out a strategy on how to win.<br /> <br /> Some key points: Caestus uses what few stats are provided for him in 1st Edition's Worldwide Phase I. I'm not including much more than that, to avoid any assumptions. All of his Quantum Powers have been placed under his Elemental Mastery due to all of them revolving around Kinetic Energy, but if you want to increase the effective XP and avoid going into multiple actions, you can separate them out like Cestus does.<ul><li>Quantum 6 (Technically lower then Cestus, but see below)</li> <li>Mega-Attributes: Might 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4, Cunning 5 (I'm combining his Perception and Wits stats for the sake of ease), Presence 1</li> <li>Mega-Edges (&quot;-&gt;&quot; Indicates where the 1st Edition and 2nd Edition names differ):<ul><li>Mega-Lifting (Can increase Might for lifting purposes), Shockwave (Can attack all characters in close range when grounded), Thunderclap (As before, but can't deal damage in exchange for use in the air), Fast Tasks -&gt; Quickness (Apply Speed Scale to Routine Tasks), Rapid Strike (Can either add Mega-Dexterity/Cunning rating as Enhancement to attacks, or attack all characters in close range), Adaptation (Immune to Indirect Environmental Damage, Doesn't need to eat, drink, breathe or sleep), Regeneration (Can rapidly heal injuries), Spectrum Vision (See in complete darkness and through objects), Quickness -&gt; Multitasking (Gain Enhancement when performing multiple actions, up to Mega-Cunning/Dexterity)</li> <li>Invulnerability (Kinetic Energy) -&gt; Toughness 5 - Restricted 1 (Kinetic Energy Only)</li> <li>Technique (Elemental Mastery) 4</li> </ul></li> <li>Quantum Powers: No ratings are given here, so this is all just assumptions:<ul><li>Elemental Mastery (Kinetic Energy) 5<ul><li>Telekinesis: Quantum Anima 5 (Duration, Grab, Might 1, Ranged, Strike)</li> <li>Quantum Bolt: Quantum Attack 5 (Ranged 3 (Long), Explosive 2)</li> <li>Claws: Quantum Attack 1 (Brutal) + Duration 4 (Instant -&gt; Continuous (Minutes))</li> <li>Flight 5</li> <li>Force Field: Quantum Field 4 + Hard Armor 1</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Most of Team Tomorrow's skillset can be seen in the Proteus Novas Companion, but as a comparison between the Pax:<ul><li>Quantum 7</li> <li>Mega-Attributes: Might 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3</li> <li>Mega-Edges:<ul><li>Mega-Crush (Can increase Might for demolition purposes), Mega-Lifting (See Above), Mega-Speed (Convert Mega-Dexterity into increased Speed Scale), Technique (Elemental Mastery) 1</li> </ul></li> <li>Quantum Powers:<ul><li>Elemental Mastery (Kinetic) 3<ul><li>Quantum Anima 3 (Duration, Manipulation, Might)</li> <li>Quantum Deflection 3</li> </ul></li> <li>Flight 5</li> <li>Quantum Attack 4 (Brutal, Piercing, Ranged 2 (Medium)</li> </ul></li> </ul>So Cestus has the edge in terms of Quantum Points, but falls behind in most other areas. Thus, taking all of this into account: Who would win? Caestus, or all of Team Tomorrow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}